fields.value:

{{Stealnotes
| name = Tempest Double
| desc = Creates a {{H|Rubick}} Double with all of his basic abilities, without other {{A|Rubick|Stolen Spell 1|text=Acquired 
Abilities}} and {{A|Rubick|Spell Steal}} inactive.<br><br>Losing and reacquiring the {{A|Arc Warden|Tempest Double}} ability allows Rubick to summon another Double from the previous ability acquisition.
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Tempest Double
| desc = Unavailable.
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Tempest Double icon0}}
| desc = Briefly refocusing its fractured elements into a single form, the Arc Warden is able to create a perfect electrical duplication of itself. The duplicate can use all of Arc Warden's current items and spells, except most consumables and items that drop on death. The duplicate has separate item and ability cooldowns.<br><br>The Tempest Double loses its sense of self and fractures over time, becoming slower and less accurate.
}}
<hr>
* {{M|The Double}} has the following additional properties:
** The {{M|gold}} bounty is also distributed evenly among creeps and {{M|buildings}} akin to hero kills when not killed by player-controlled units.
** Ultimate abilities are always inactive on The Double.
** The {{M|clone}} spawn distance is defined as:
*** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|Caster[[Collision Size|ColSize]] × 2 + 2)}}
*** For The Self, The Double spawns at a random position {{Code|{{#expr:{{G|collision size hero}}*2+2}}-distance}} away.
** The Double is always created with The Self's current basic abilities' and updates its ability level accordingly upon cast.

